      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Mixing too much caffeine with your Ritalin can be risky and unpredictable since both can affect your nervous system. Over-the-counter energy pills or multiple doses of high-caffeine energy drinks might overstimulate you, potentially leading to erratic periods of focus with subsequent crashes. Side effects might not be immediately apparent, but they can include jitteriness, insomnia, and reduced ability to concentrate later. Safe study strategies include timed breaks, proper sleep, maintaining regular hydration, and possibly trying other methods like the Pomodoro Technique, mindfulness exercises, or short physical activity breaks for sustained focus. It's crucial to prioritize overall well-being rather than short-term boost, as this will be more helpful in the long run, especially during exam stress.",
